{"name":"Holy Grail","hex":"#e8d720","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Holy Grail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An artifact in Arthurian mythology, being in later versions the cup used by Christ at the Last Supper and in which some of his blood was caught during the crucifixion.","A web page layout with fixed-width columns to the left and right, and a central area that fills the remaining space."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Anything that is highly sought-after but attained only through a difficult endeavor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Holy_Grail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holy Grail","blocks":[{"text":"The Holy Grail is a treasure that serves as an important motif in Arthurian literature. Various traditions describe the Holy Grail as a cup, dish, or stone with miraculous healing powers, sometimes providing eternal youth or sustenance in infinite abundance, often guarded in the custody of the Fisher King and located in the hidden Grail castle. By analogy, any elusive object or goal of great significance may be perceived as a \"holy grail\" by those seeking such."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg/330px-Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Grail"},{"title":"Holy Grail (Jay-Z song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Holy Grail\" is a song by American rapper Jay-Z from his twelfth studio album Magna Carta Holy Grail. It features vocals from American singer Justin Timberlake and serves as the album's lead single. It was produced by The-Dream, Timbaland, and J-Roc, with additional production from No I.D. and contains elements of Nirvana's 1991 single \"Smells Like Teen Spirit\". Lyrically, \"Holy Grail\" finds both performers discussing the hardships of fame."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Grail_(Jay-Z_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg/500px-Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg/500px-Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_%281874%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_The_Damsel_of_the_Sanct_Grael_(1874).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Edward_Burne-Jones_-_The_Attainment%3B_The_Vision_of_the_Holy_Grail_to_Sir_Galahad%2C_Sir_Bors_and_Sir_Percival_%28from_the_series_%27The_Quest_for_the_Holy_Grail%27%29.jpg/500px-Edward_Burne-Jones_-_The_Attainment%3B_The_Vision_of_the_Holy_Grail_to_Sir_Galahad%2C_Sir_Bors_and_Sir_Percival_%28from_the_series_%27The_Quest_for_the_Holy_Grail%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Edward_Burne-Jones_-_The_Attainment%3B_The_Vision_of_the_Holy_Grail_to_Sir_Galahad%2C_Sir_Bors_and_Sir_Percival_%28from_the_series_%27The_Quest_for_the_Holy_Grail%27%29.jpg/500px-Edward_Burne-Jones_-_The_Attainment%3B_The_Vision_of_the_Holy_Grail_to_Sir_Galahad%2C_Sir_Bors_and_Sir_Percival_%28from_the_series_%27The_Quest_for_the_Holy_Grail%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Galahad, Percival and Bors achieve the Grail. Tapestry woven by Morris & Co. (19th century)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdward_Burne-Jones_-_The_Attainment%3B_The_Vision_of_the_Holy_Grail_to_Sir_Galahad%2C_Sir_Bors_and_Sir_Percival_(from